%S A259824 1,1,1,1,2,2,1,3,6,4,1,4,13,16,8,1,5,24,46,40,16,1,6,40,114,140,96,32,
%T A259824 1,7,62,256,424,392,224,64,1,8,91,534,1180,1368,1040,512,128,1,9,128,
%U A259824 1050,3088,4392,4064,2656,1152,256,1,10,174,1965,7692,13360,14496,11424,6592,2560,512
%N A259824 A Catalan-type triangle read by rows, generated by iteration of convolution squares.
%C A259824 The triangle is generated by an iterative procedure in which the (n+1)-st row of the following array is the convolution square of the n-th row prepended with a 1.
%C A259824   1, 1, 1,  1,  1,  1,   1, ...(given)
%C A259824   1, 2, 3,  4,  5,  6,   7, ...
%C A259824   1, 2, 5, 10, 18, 30,  47, ...
%C A259824   1, 2, 5, 14, 34, 76, 161, ...
%C A259824   ...
%C A259824 where the rows converge to the Catalan numbers (A000108).
%C A259824 Example: second row of (1, 2, 3, ...) is prepended with a 1: (1, 1, 2, 3, ...), and the convolution square of that sequence is row 3 (1, 2, 5, 10, 18, ...).
%C A259824 Next, take finite differences of terms by columns; such that the finite difference row of the n-th column becomes the n-th row of the triangle. First few rows of the triangle (as an infinite lower triangular matrix with the rest zeros) are:
%C A259824   1;
%C A259824   1, 1;
%C A259824   1, 2, 2;
%C A259824   1, 3, 6, 4;
%C A259824   1, 4, 13, 16, 8;
%C A259824   1, 5, 24, 46, 40, 16;
%C A259824   1, 6, 40, 114, 140, 96, 32;
%C A259824   1, 7, 62, 256, 424, 392, 224, 64;
%C A259824   ...
%e A259824 Row 4 of the triangle is (1, 3, 6, 4, 0, 0, 0, ...) since the finite differences of row 4 of the array (1, 4, 10, 14, 14, ...) are (1, 3, 6, 4, 0, 0, 0, ...).
%o A259824 (PARI) T(n,k) = my(f=1/(1-x)+O(x^n), g=0); for(r=2, k, g=f; f=(1+x*f)^2); polcoef(f-g, n-1);
%o A259824 row(n) = vector(n, k, T(n,k)); \\ _Alper Ferudun_, Oct 11 2026
%o A259824 (Python)
%o A259824 def A259824_row(n):
%o A259824     a, col = [1]*n, [1]
%o A259824     for _ in range(n-1):
%o A259824         p = [1] + a[:n-1]
%o A259824         a = [sum(p[i]*p[k-i] for i in range(k+1)) for k in range(n)]
%o A259824         col.append(a[n-1])
%o A259824     return [col[0]] + [col[i]-col[i-1] for i in range(1, n)] # _Alper Ferudun_, Oct 11 2026
%Y A259824 Cf. A000108 (row sums).
%K A259824 nonn,tabl,changed
